title: White Noise System (ses-sistemi)
message: >-
  If you use this software in work that you publish, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: İsmail
    family-names: Özyurt
    email: ismailozyurt96@gmail.com
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/theiozyurt/ses-sistemi'
abstract: >-
  A calibrated, schedule-driven white-noise generator for laboratory
  use. Delivers continuous synthetic white noise through a selected
  audio output for a timed program, including repeating work/rest
  cycles, with meter-anchored sound pressure level estimates and
  sleep inhibition for unattended multi-hour runs. Built as the
  acoustic stressor delivery module of a chronic unpredictable mild
  stress (CUMS) protocol in rats (Kütahya Health Sciences University
  Animal Experiments Local Ethics Committee, decision no. 2026.07.02).
keywords:
  - white noise
  - acoustic stressor
  - chronic unpredictable mild stress
  - CUMS
  - animal behaviour
  - laboratory automation
  - psychoacoustics
